  "id": "COMPOUND:26998 - PROTEIN:6147",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between the compound (+)-(5S,7R)-7-Ethoxy-12-Hydroxy-2-Oxo-20-Norabieta-1(10),8,11,13-Tetraene and Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, all of which involve the compound interacting with a common target, CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase. This enzyme is targeted by three distinct compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, which in turn target the SDR family member 9. The shared target and the presence of multiple compounds that interact with the same enzyme suggest a potential mechanism of action involving the SDR family member 9, possibly through a common pathway or a shared functional role in metabolic processes. The evidence is consistent and supports a biologically plausible mechanism, though further investigation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction and its relevance to the compound's therapeutic effects.",
